From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:02:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Keep render microsequences in
 ASC-cached session slots by default

Each render's TA and FS microsequences are rewritten at every publication
and read by the firmware's interpreter while it prepares and starts each
stage. In their per-VM sequence objects they are mapped uncached, and the
interpreter's work per stage is about twice macOS's, which maps them
ASC-cached.

Make g16_render_seq_pool default to 1 and g16_render_seq_cached default to
1. Every render then writes its microsequences into its unit's slot in the
ASC-cached session object, two objects of 18 units of 8 KiB each for the
whole device. Render units are claimed device-wide, so no two renders in
flight share a slot, and the firmware cleans and invalidates each stage's
sequence when it prepares the stage and again at its post.

On the J604 the cached copy took render.light at depth 64 from 82.7 and
83.5 us to 77.0 us, depth 1 10.5 % and depth 8 4.7 % faster, with fill and
geometry rows within 0.1 %, pixels and readback hash unchanged and both
stress tests passing.

g16_render_seq_cached=0 at run time returns to the uncached copy, and
aurora.g16_render_seq_pool=0 on the command line to each unit's own
sequence objects.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs | 4 ++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
index 54a7442859..342fe00ce1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
@@ -292,8 +292,8 @@ fn init(module: &'static kernel::ThisModule) -> impl PinInit<Self, Error> {
             description: "G16: 1 queue 2 compute 4 TA 8 FS 16 ring; 32/64/128 work/seq/barrier",
         },
         g16_render_seq_pool: u32 {
-            default: 0,
-            description: "G16: 1 = render microsequences in session slots per unit, uncached and ASC-cached copies",
+            default: 1,
+            description: "G16: 1 (default) = render microsequences in session slots per unit, uncached and ASC-cached copies; 0 = each unit's own sequence objects",
         },
         g16_host_records: u32 {
             default: 0,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 986ea76f53..6fed215f49 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -709,7 +709,7 @@ pub(crate) fn fw_cached_mask() -> u32 {
     module_parameters::g16_fw_cached.value()
 }
 
-/// `g16_render_seq_pool` (load time, default 0). 1: at boot two session objects, one uncached
+/// `g16_render_seq_pool` (load time, default 1). 1: at boot two session objects, one uncached
 /// and one ASC-cached, each hold one TA and one FS microsequence slot per render unit, and every
 /// render writes its live microsequences into its unit's slot instead of the unit's per-VM
 /// sequence objects. Render units are claimed device-wide, so no two VMs use a slot at once, and
@@ -719,8 +719,8 @@ pub(crate) fn render_seq_pool() -> bool {
     module_parameters::g16_render_seq_pool.value() == 1
 }
 
-/// Storage of `g16_render_seq_cached` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static RENDER_SEQ_CACHED: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_render_seq_cached` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static RENDER_SEQ_CACHED: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// With `g16_render_seq_pool`, whether renders published from now on name the ASC-cached copy of
 /// their unit's microsequence slot (attribute index 0, the class macOS gives these objects)
@@ -736,7 +736,7 @@ pub(crate) fn render_seq_cached() -> bool {
     RENDER_SEQ_CACHED_PARM,
     RENDER_SEQ_CACHED,
     "g16_render_seq_cached",
-    "G16: with g16_render_seq_pool=1, publish renders with the ASC-cached copy of their unit's microsequence slot (default 0: the uncached copy; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: with g16_render_seq_pool=1, publish renders with the ASC-cached copy of their unit's microsequence slot (default 1; 0: the uncached copy; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// `g16_ktrace_mask` (load time): the word written to CONTROL+0 at init. 25G83 copies it into
-- 
2.43.0

